<?xml version="1.0"?>
<rdf:RDF xmlns="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/componency.owl#"
     xml:base="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/componency.owl"
     xmlns:owl="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#"
     xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#"
     xmlns:xml="http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace"
     xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#"
     xmlns:rdfs="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#"
     xmlns:skos="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#"
     xmlns:partof="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/partof.owl#"
     xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/"
     xmlns:componency="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/componency.owl#"
     xmlns:cpannotationschema="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl#">
    <owl:Ontology rdf:about="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/componency.owl">
        <owl:imports rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/partof.owl"/>
        <dcterms:description rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">To represent (non-transitively) that entities either are proper parts of other entities, or have proper parts.</dcterms:description>
        <dcterms:title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Componency Pattern</dcterms:title>
        <cpannotationschema:coversRequirements>What is this entity component of? What are the components of this entity?</cpannotationschema:coversRequirements>
        <cpannotationschema:extractedFrom>http://ontologydesignpatterns.org/ont/dul/DUL.owl</cpannotationschema:extractedFrom>
        <cpannotationschema:hasConsequences>This Content OP allows designers to represent part-whole relations. It allows to distinguish between parts and proper parts. Relation of proper part is not transitive, and implies a simple  part of relation, which is transitive. Temporal indexing is not expressible. To solve this issue see the  time indexed part of Content OP. </cpannotationschema:hasConsequences>
        <cpannotationschema:hasIntent rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">To represent (non-transitively) that entities either are proper parts of other entities, or have proper parts.</cpannotationschema:hasIntent>
        <cpannotationschema:isSpecializationOf>PartOf</cpannotationschema:isSpecializationOf>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Curated by OntoBoard 1.155.0, so that the pattern passes ODK&apos;s quality report with its default profile, names every term with a label, and is consistent and coherent. Changes: label added x9; term declared x2;
- header: dcterms:title &quot;Componency Pattern&quot; - the library&apos;s name for the pattern
- header: dcterms:description - the library&apos;s description of the pattern
Each change is listed under &quot;curated&quot; in the pattern&apos;s metadata.json in OntoBoard&apos;s pattern library.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment>The componency pattern, without temporal indexing. 
This pattern re-uses the part of pattern and is extracted from DOLCE-UltraLite by partial clone.</rdfs:comment>
        <owl:versionInfo rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">1.1 added rdfs:isDefinedBy for all named entities</owl:versionInfo>
        <owl:versionInfo rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Created by Adlo Gangemi</owl:versionInfo>
    </owl:Ontology>
    


